From bc2f1dfb1909504b9ee2424783086982b067fc50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:19:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Continue camera framing when movement starts immediately

Continue already computes and uploads the saved view synchronously. Do not
queue a second fixed-target pan after that work. With asynchronous tile bands,
the pan can hold camera follow for 52 ticks while the tamer walks away; when
follow resumes, its per-step delta cannot recover the missed movement.

The Green Gym left-walk fixture reproduces this on v0.0.7 and main but keeps
the tamer visible on vanilla or when movement waits until the pan completes.
Remove the redundant pan instead of adding resident state or disabling field
input. Scripted pans retain their existing path.

---
 src/main/main.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/main.c b/src/main/main.c
index 978679aa..e6e300ee 100644
--- a/src/main/main.c
+++ b/src/main/main.c
@@ -3882,8 +3882,6 @@ extern int8_t TAMER_PREVIOUS_TILE_X;
 extern int8_t TAMER_PREVIOUS_TILE_Y;
 extern int8_t TAMER_WAYPOINT_CURRENT;
 extern int8_t TAMER_WAYPOINT_ACTIVE;
-extern int32_t CAMERA_UPDATE_TILES;
-void createCameraMovement(VECTOR *target, int32_t instanceId);
 void setImmortalHour(void);
 extern int8_t PREV_TILE_X;
 extern int8_t PREV_TILE_Y;
@@ -3978,8 +3976,9 @@ void initializeLoadedMap(void)
 	TAMER_START_TILE_X = SAVED_STATE.tamerStartTileX;
 	TAMER_START_TILE_Y = SAVED_STATE.tamerStartTileY;
 	TAMER_WAYPOINT_ACTIVE = SAVED_STATE.tamerWaypointActive;
-	CAMERA_UPDATE_TILES = 1;
-	createCameraMovement(&TAMER_ENTITY.entity.posData->location, 2);
+	/* Position and upload the final saved view below before field control.
+	 * A second, queued pan keeps aiming at this snapshot while the tamer
+	 * walks; asynchronous camera bands can then leave him outside the view. */
 	setImmortalHour();
 	initializeDrawingOffsets(MAP_TILE_DATA.tiles);
 
